# Trivy vulnerability suppressions
# Reviewed: 2026-06-29 — re-review by: 2026-09-29
#
# Only findings that are BOTH (a) not reachable in our usage AND (b) have no feasible
# fix belong here. Everything fixable has been fixed (see docs/security-scan-2026-06-29.md).

# ecdsa — CVE-2024-23342 (Minerva timing side-channel in python-ecdsa).
# No upstream fix exists (python-ecdsa upstream declines to fix). Pulled transitively by
# python-jose. We sign/verify tokens with RS256 only (api/src/config/auth.py:
# SIGNING_ALGORITHM = "RS256"), so the EC (ecdsa) code path is never exercised.
CVE-2024-23342

# langchain-core — CVE-2026-34070 (path traversal in legacy load_prompt /
# load_prompt_from_config). Fixed only in langchain-core 1.2.22 (langchain 1.x major
# upgrade — tracked as a separate migration). We do not call load_prompt /
# load_prompt_from_config anywhere, so the vulnerable path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-34070
